==English==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|courteous||lang=enm|courtly}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|cort||lang=fro|court}}, from {{etyl|la}}, displaced native {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|hende||courteous, gracious, friendly|lang=ang}}.


===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GB}} {{IPA|/ˈkɜːtiəs/}}
* {{audio|en-us-courteous.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Showing [[regard]] or [[thought]] for others; especially, displaying good [[manners]] or [[etiquette]].
#: ''a '''courteous''' gentleman''
#: ''a '''courteous''' gesture''

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:polite]]

